      "text": "To find the number of distinct numbers in the list \\(\\left\\lfloor \\frac{1^2}{1000} \\right\\rfloor, \\ \\left\\lfloor \\frac{2^2}{1000} \\right\\rfloor, \\ \\left\\lfloor \\frac{3^2}{1000} \\right\\rfloor, \\ \\dots, \\ \\left\\lfloor \\frac{1000^2}{1000} \\right\\rfloor\\), we need to determine the range and number of unique values that the expression \\(\\left\\lfloor \\frac{n^2}{1000} \\right\\rfloor\\) takes for \\(n\\) ranging from 1 to 1000.\n\nFirst, let's find the minimum and maximum values of \\(\\left\\lfloor \\frac{n^2}{1000} \\right\\rfloor\\).\n\n- The minimum value occurs when \\(n^2\\) is just less than \\(1000\\).\n  \\[\n  \\left\\lfloor \\frac{1^2}{1000} \\right\\rfloor = \\left\\lfloor \\frac{1}{1000} \\right\\rfloor = 0\n  \\]\n  \\[\n  \\left\\lfloor \\frac{2^2}{1000} \\right\\rfloor = \\left\\lfloor \\frac{4}{1000} \\right\\rfloor = \\left\\lfloor 0.004 \\right\\rfloor = 0\n  \\]\n  \\[\n  \\left\\lfloor \\frac{999^2}{1000} \\right\\rfloor = \\left\\lfloor \\frac{998001}{1000} \\right\\rfloor = \\left\\lfloor 998.001 \\right\\rfloor = 998\n  \\]\n  Therefore, the minimum value of \\(\\left\\lfloor \\frac{n^2}{1000} \\right\\rfloor\\) is 0.\n\n- The maximum value occurs when \\(n^2\\) is just greater than \\(1000^2\\).\n  \\[\n  \\left\\lfloor \\frac{1000^2}{1000} \\right\\rfloor = \\left\\lfloor 10000 \\right\\rfloor = 10000\n  \\]\n  Therefore, the maximum value of \\(\\left\\lfloor \\frac{n^2}{1000} \\right\\rfloor\\) is 10000.\n\nThe distinct values of \\(\\left\\lfloor \\frac{n^2}{1000} \\right\\rfloor\\) are all integers from 0 to 10000 inclusive. To find the number of distinct values, we calculate:\n\\[\n10000 - 0 + 1 = 10001\n\\]\n\nThus, the number of distinct numbers in the list is \\(\\boxed{10001}\\).",
